    "name": "Harishchandragad",
    "category": "trek",
    "lat": 19.3833,
    "lng": 73.7667,
    "region": "Base village Khireshwar, Ahmednagar",
    "description": "A demanding climb to an ancient hill fort, famous for the Konkan Kada cliff and the Kedareshwar cave temple.",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "altitude_m": 1424,
    "duration_label": "7-8 hr one way",
    "best_season": "Oct-Feb",
    "highlights": [
      "Konkan Kada — a massive concave cliff, rare \"sun's halo\" cloud effect at sunrise",
      "Kedareshwar cave — giant Shivling ringed by knee-deep water",
      "Popular overnight-camping summit under a wide-open night sky"
    ],
    "distance_from_mumbai_km": 165,
    "distance_from_pune_km": 145,
    "time_by_car_minutes": 220,
    "time_by_bike_minutes": 260,
    "how_to_reach": "Base villages Khireshwar or Pachnai, reached via Kalyan-Ahmednagar road.",
    "nearest_station": "Igatpuri Railway Station — 38 km; taxis run on to Khireshwar base village.",
    "things_to_carry": ["Trekking shoes", "Headlamp", "2L water", "Warm layer"],
    "safety_note": "Konkan Kada's edge has no railing and gets foggy — stay well back, especially at dawn. The Pachnai route has a risky rock-patch in the rains.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Is Harishchandragad safe for beginners?",
        "answer": "No — it's rated hard. The Konkan Kada cliff and the long approach make it unsuitable for first-time trekkers."
      },
      {
        "question": "How long does the trek take?",
        "answer": "7-8 hours one way from Khireshwar or Pachnai; most groups make it an overnight trek."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is water available on the trail?",
        "answer": "Yes, near Kedareshwar cave and at the top — but carry your own for the climb up."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I drive close to the base?",
        "answer": "Yes — both Khireshwar and Pachnai villages are motorable; the trek starts from there."
      },
      {
        "question": "Best time to visit?",
        "answer": "October to February for clear views. Avoid monsoon — the rock sections get slippery."
      }
    ],
